From b636c7f593a0926059e63906f1e118370adf82e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:03:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07253/11362] [outer-loop] fix sc25 live drift confirmed;
 re-validate all 25 games live; find + root-cause a new lf52 live gap

Operator: "Fix the sc25 drift and re-validate all games."

PART 1 (the requested scope): the sc25 live drift was already root-caused and
fixed in an earlier session (commit a09892c5a, a missing WARMUP_GAMES step --
sc25's first env.step after reset is silently consumed as a no-op) but never
re-tested live -- the fix landed 18 minutes AFTER the failed 2026-07-15 run
that diagnosed it. Ran scripts/arc3_live_submit.py (VALIDATE mode, no
--submit, no scorecard close, no leaderboard record) against the real live
ARC-AGI-3 API: 25/25 games now env-match live, sc25 confirmed fixed
(claimed L5 -> LIVE L5 MATCH, scorecard 9f4c282d...).

PART 2 (bonus, beyond the literal ask): that run used the existing package
(experiment_4679..., stale since 2026-06-24), which caps bp35/lf52 at L1 --
far below their true same-day depth (bp35 9/9, lf52 10/10, both solved
earlier today). Since fully-verified flat action sequences for both already
existed, replayed them live directly on a fresh scorecard to test whether
today's offline wins hold on the real environment:

- bp35: CLEAN MATCH. Claimed L9, LIVE L9, all 410 actions replayed with zero
  errors (163s). The live path handles this game's full win fine.
- lf52: FAILED, but with a fully diagnosed root cause. An instrumented
  per-action re-run confirmed correct live level progress through L8
  (827/1009 actions, all 8 transitions at the exact expected indices), then
  a clean HTTP 400 at action 849. The L9 tail clicks pixel x=132 -- outside
  the live frame's valid 0-63 range -- to directly address an off-screen
  blue-peg pair (source grid x=21, matching this game's own registry gotcha
  describing exactly this off-screen-relay maneuver as part of the L9 win).
  22 such out-of-bounds clicks exist in the L9-L10 tail; zero in the L1-L8
  prefix, which is exactly why L8 replays clean and L9 doesn't. The offline
  arc_agi arcade accepts and routes out-of-bounds ACTION6 clicks; the live
  API validates strictly and rejects them. This is a real, structural
  offline/live permissiveness gap -- not a driver bug, not a warmup-step
  issue like sc25, and not something to patch in the same turn it was found.
  Does NOT retract lf52's offline 10/10 registry credit (independently
  verified earlier today, unaffected by this live-API difference); DOES mean
  lf52's live-submittable depth is currently L8, not L10, until an in-bounds
  equivalent route is found -- genuine new exploration, flagged as the
  sharpest concrete lead for the new Generalization-Testing Floor's task
  class 2, not attempted here.

Updated ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: backfilled the 2026-07-15 run that was
never added to the live_submissions history, added both 2026-07-17 runs, and
added an honest live_replay_status field to lf52's own game entry so the
caveat is discoverable without reading the full diagnostic artifact.

Full evidence: results/outer_loop_live_revalidation_20260717.json
(adversarial-verify clean), results/arc3_live_validate_deep_wins_20260717.json,
results/arc3_live_submit.json (fresh run output).

